    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The kingdom grew from the union of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#svear">Svear</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#uppsala">Uppsala</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#geats">Geats</a> of the south-west around the year 1000.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gustavus-adolphus">Gustav II Adolf</a> and his successors it became the dominant Baltic power, winning German lands at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#westphalia">Westphalia</a> in 1648.</li><li>Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709 ended its empire; after 1814 it kept out of war and built a model welfare state.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sveriges-riksbank">Riksbank</a>, founded in 1668, is the oldest central bank still in operation, and its predecessor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#stockholms-banco">Stockholms Banco</a> issued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>’s first banknotes in 1661.</p></aside>
    </section>

